{
  "description": "Engine shots of the demo video, rendered by scripts/demo-footage.ts (npm run demo:footage) into out/video/<id>/frame_0001.png …, out/video/<id>.mp4 and out/video/contact_sheet.png. Unreal, Blender, terminal and MCP shots are screen captures and are not listed. kind: orbit = one cook, the camera turns by degrees_per_frame from azimuth; sequence = the frames cooked in order (simulation state carries over); still = one frame held for seconds. render takes the keys of an example's meta.render (src/render/options.ts). set changes the graph in memory (dotted paths) instead of editing the example. pane: the right half of the 1920 x 1080 timeline; frames are centred in it with bands of the render footer colour above and below for captions, unless crop is given ([width, height, top edge] of the frame for a full-frame shot). left: the graph JSON shown in the left pane, written verbatim to out/video/<id>/left.txt.",
  "fps": 30,
  "pane": [960, 1080],
  "shots": [
    {
      "id": "s01_title_bg",
      "plan": "shot 1, 0:00-0:10: title card background (dim it in the edit)",
